th  these antibodies from both approaches  compared to benchmark antibodies the  sensograms of a benchmark and top two  clones from beacon platform are  shown on the right side here  as you can see that these and two  antibodies look similar to benchmark  antibody  a very fast on rate and slow  dissociation curve  we actually had uh several antibodies  from b cell cloning campaign  that had a single-digit nanomolar  affinity  or better  so overall we can say that  a beacon platform certainly gave us the  really good output  so here is a summary of the  antibodies that we were able to obtain  from  a b-cell cloning and hybridoma approach  overall as you can see from the  hierarchical crossring tree  that the most of the antibodies were  unique and randy and  distant from the benchmark but i  definitely wanted to point out that the  two antibodies that  had a  uh really good affinity which are  listed in this green box are unique as  well as distant from the  the the four benchmarks that we  tested they are also listed in the red  box  and i also wanted to mention that  we noticed that we had  all the antibodies  from b cell cloning approach had 100  unique sequence  uh unlike the hyperdoma where sometimes  the  dominant clone takes over the other  clones and your diversity  may be lower  compared to the b cell cloning  so this is a slide basically summarizing  the evaluation of the  antibodies obtained from  both campaigns b-cell cloning and  hybridoma  so overall we can say  that there are a number of factors that  needed to be  considered  uh certainly  the time that it takes to to get these  sequences two to four months for beacon  platform in comparison with eight to ten  months in  uh hyperdoma approach  the selection  criteria is extremely important  because uh  in beacon platform we use  a very clear image based  selection  where we look for the negative signal  for the uh  for the soluble liquid in case uh in  here  in the fitzy channel  compared to the hybri