con so as uh earlier in  the talk i have already explained you  what type of acids that are done the  most common acids that are requested are  the in channel acids you can do the  binding assay cross reactive assay  multi cloud cross reactive assay  multiplex format  uh you can also do the cell based uh  cell based assay  uh sequentially if you have multiple  uh cell lines to screen against you can  also do  in pen cell binding and  and uh eat based in channel assay uh  combined so there are multiple ways of  of doing the  this assay on beacon  and we have certainly tested a couple of  different configurations that have  worked  on number of projects that we have done  in past  uh we have also done the in pen binding  and blocking acid which is also seem to  be very popular certainly because you  can identify the  uh potential candidates having that  blocking activity early on  and recently our projects also been  focused on these uh reporter assays  where we were able to identify certain  certain clones which basically activates  the pathway and that was basically  uh  seen in in form of gfp signal over  a certain time so those kinds of assays  are also  uh can be done on on beacon platform  okay and the next question is what is  the overall recovery and diversity of  the clones  the overall recovery in our experience  is is typically around 80 percent uh so  we have basically uh  uh basically have let's say about  hundred  uh hits from beacon there is also an  attrition rate  uh from from the identified hit up to  the  getting the sequences of them at certain  stage typically our cdna recovery is  really good as it is around like 95  but at some times you would probably  lose some of the clones during the vh  and vl amplification  stage as well as  as well as the sequencing stage so  typically we in our experience we were  able to recover around 80 percent of the  clones  and uh the the good thing about is the  whatever clones that we were able to  recover had th